==English==

===Etymology===
Medical term; from {{AGr.}} [[αἷμα]] ([[blood]]) + [[φιλία]] ([[friendship]])

===Pronunciation===
* Rhymes: [[Rhymes:English:-ɪliə|-ɪliə]]

===Alternative spellings===
'''hemophilia'''

===Noun===
'''haemophilia'''

# {{pathology}} Any of several hereditary illnesses that impair the body's ability to control bleeding, usually passed from mother to son.

====Synonyms====
* [[bleeder's disease]]
* [[Christmas disease]]

